From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:21:08 -0643
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zumapro-tegu: Add the Kepler GNSS
 link

The Pixel 9a's GNSS receiver is the Kepler core in its S5300 modem. Its
data go over an SPI bus of the application processor, USI3 of HSI0
(spi21), in 64-byte blocks paced by two handshake lines; gnssif_spi
drives both. Add the SPI device and the handshake node, and enable the
USI.

The bus keeps zumapro's port configuration, with which spi-s3c64xx
moves a 64-byte block in one piece. With gs101's compatible alone
(the controller's automatic chip select, as stock uses for this
device) the driver cut each block into 60 and 4 bytes, and in two
sessions on the phone 12 of those reads timed out (-110) in 13
minutes; with zumapro's, two more sessions had none. The feedback
delay is stock's 0. The bus has no pin group: it runs on the
bootloader's pin state, which the data were clean with.

Nothing probes until the modules load, and the core answers only while
the modem is up and the GNSS daemon has loaded its firmware.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts   | 36 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
index 764142419..92b6ddd37 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
@@ -53,6 +53,17 @@ A1_IPOP {
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The handshake lines of the Kepler GNSS core in the S5300 modem
+	 * (its SPI device is on spi21): the core's request to the host,
+	 * which is also the host's interrupt, and the host's request to it.
+	 */
+	gnss {
+		compatible = "samsung,exynos-gnss";
+		gnss2ap-spi-gpios = <&gpa5 4 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		ap2gnss-spi-gpios = <&gpp2 3 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	};
+
 	gpio-keys {
 		compatible = "gpio-keys";
 
@@ -779,6 +790,27 @@ touchscreen@0 {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * The Kepler GNSS core's data link, 64-byte blocks on USI3 of HSI0. The bus
+ * keeps zumapro's port configuration: a 64-byte block then moves in one
+ * piece (with gs101's, the controller driver cuts it into 60 and 4 bytes,
+ * and the second piece sometimes times out). Feedback delay 0 is stock's.
+ * The bus has no pin group and runs on the bootloader's pin state.
+ */
+&spi21 {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	gnss@0 {
+		compatible = "samsung,gnss-spi";
+		reg = <0>;
+		spi-max-frequency = <3125000>;
+
+		controller-data {
+			samsung,spi-feedback-delay = <0>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 &sysreg_apm {
 	status = "okay";
 };
@@ -876,6 +908,10 @@ &usi2_hsi0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&usi3_hsi0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &usi4 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
